      "files": [
        {
          "path": "proj/src/input/input.c",
          "originalSha256": "e454e79c9bfcda8c39740feb44d970943c09b0c29f7f16f24dfd4e2a52ef1a5d",
          "patchedSha256": "27ccd7c8ed02ab39964d70f3f8346f8454f69c4fd56f7147b4fa8c8300f4648e",
          "reason": "Match the mouse controller byte_index definition (uint8_t) in the gameplay input handler. Reading/writing it as int also consumes adjacent packet bytes and prevents pointer updates. Issue #11."
        },
        {
          "path": "proj/src/menu/local_or_remote.c",
          "originalSha256": "470f609d5a32b6be1e2a4dd162892c597cd42c2f403c685e6a6ad6e079c60b45",
          "patchedSha256": "c322394146cd680f3c5cd506d2fb12848fcaaeeeb30db373969316ba32a419bf",
          "reason": "Match the mouse controller byte_index definition (uint8_t) in the local/remote menu. The widened read prevents complete packet recognition and makes the local duel option unselectable. Issue #11."
        },
        {
          "path": "proj/src/controllers/gpu/gpu.c",
          "originalSha256": "add5eba151ce097295a659445b847da2e3e6fd14684d8834c422215af29272a6",
          "patchedSha256": "42880d2680715291be3642591315f4437f40c50478e5a15598a4da0a83f4c982",
          "reason": "Clip pixel writes to the actual framebuffer dimensions and write exactly the current pixel format byte count. Original32-bit stores overran24-bit last pixels, and the partially clipped32x32 cursor could write beyond the buffer at logical1129,839. Preserve logical pointer/aim positions and original RGB packing."
        }
      ],
      "reproduction": "Public vg_init/vg_draw_pixel regression uses an independently guarded4x3x24-bit framebuffer. Original final-pixel write corrupts the first guardbyte; removing onlyXYguard also reproduces offscreen framebuffer/guard changes. Both pass after clipping/exactbytewrite. Original logicalcursor1129,839 and directprofile unchanged."
    }
  ],
